Subject: [PATCH] old-configure: treat aarch64-apple-ios like darwin

js/src/old-configure.in's `case "$target"` Darwin branches only match
*-darwin*, so our aarch64-apple-ios target falls through to the generic
ELF defaults. Most visibly, MOZ_FIX_LINK_PATHS keeps its default GNU
"-Wl,-rpath-link,..." form, which cctools ld64 rejects ("ld: unknown option:
-rpath-link"); the Darwin branch would empty it (and set -dead_strip /
DSO_LDOPTS / libSystem handling). Extend the three darwin case patterns to
also match *-ios*. (moz.configure's linker logic already keys on
kernel==Darwin, which iOS is, so only the autoconf layer needs this.)

--- a/js/src/old-configure.in
+++ b/js/src/old-configure.in
@@ -287,7 +287,7 @@
     esac
     ;;

-*-darwin*)
+*-darwin*|*-ios*)
     HOST_CFLAGS="$HOST_CFLAGS -DXP_UNIX -DXP_MACOSX"
     HOST_OPTIMIZE_FLAGS="${HOST_OPTIMIZE_FLAGS=-O3}"
     ;;
@@ -308,7 +308,7 @@
 dnl ========================================================

 case "$target" in
-*-darwin*)
+*-darwin*|*-ios*)
     MOZ_OPTIMIZE_FLAGS="-O3"
     DSO_LDOPTS=''

@@ -563,7 +563,7 @@
 dnl they both are just symlinks to libSystem and explicitly linking
 dnl against libSystem causes issues when debugging (see bug 299601).
 case $target in
-*-darwin*)
+*-darwin*|*-ios*)
     ;;
 *)
     AC_SEARCH_LIBS(dlopen, dl,
